00:58:50,700 --> 00:58:51,900
Should we move together as a pair?

1356
00:58:51,900 --> 00:58:53,500
I'll move together with Korone.

1357
00:58:53,500 --> 00:58:54,900
Wait, seriously?! That much?!

1358
00:58:54,900 --> 00:58:56,700
Staff Buddy too!

1359
00:58:56,700 --> 00:58:58,300
Then I guess Flare will go solo.

1360
00:58:58,300 --> 00:58:59,300
Ahahahaha!

1361
00:58:59,300 --> 00:59:00,900
Wait, that's not IRyS!

1362
00:59:00,900 --> 00:59:03,300
Ahahahaha!

1363
00:59:03,300 --> 00:59:05,500
We can't let both of us get taken out at once.

1364
00:59:05,500 --> 00:59:05,900
True.

1365
00:59:05,900 --> 00:59:08,300
I'll go while protecting IRyS.

1366
00:59:08,300 --> 00:59:09,900
Which way do we go?

1367
00:59:09,900 --> 00:59:11,900
Protect me~!

1368
00:59:12,800 --> 00:59:14,000
Yes! Got one!

1369
00:59:14,000 --> 00:59:15,000
Nice!

1370
00:59:15,000 --> 00:59:16,000
That felt great!

1371
00:59:17,800 --> 00:59:19,600
She's already pulling her weight!

1372
00:59:19,600 --> 00:59:20,600
Amazing~

1373
00:59:21,900 --> 00:59:25,000
I have nothing left to teach IRyS.

1374
00:59:25,000 --> 00:59:26,850
That's a bit premature.

1375
00:59:29,300 --> 00:59:31,420
Oh no! Ugh! Getting wrecked by the Inkbrush!

1376
00:59:31,420 --> 00:59:32,400
That was close!

1377
00:59:32,400 --> 00:59:34,200
Someone's in! Someone's in! Nice!

1378
00:59:34,200 --> 00:59:36,000
Oh, nice.

1379
00:59:36,000 --> 00:59:37,800
Sorry, oh, IRyS—

1380
00:59:37,800 --> 00:59:39,800
I lost track and then I was dead.

1381
00:59:41,600 --> 00:59:43,400
I'm so sorry!

1382
00:59:45,490 --> 00:59:47,490
I'm heading to the center.

1383
00:59:50,040 --> 00:59:52,040
Me too, center.

1384
00:59:52,840 --> 00:59:55,840
Someone coming from the right, from the right!

1385
00:59:55,840 --> 00:59:58,640
One coming from the right — one — they've got a brush.

1386
00:59:58,640 --> 01:00:00,640
From the right — got them, got them!

1387
01:00:00,640 --> 01:00:02,640
Nice, nice!

1388
01:00:03,450 --> 01:00:05,310
They're using bombs!

1389
01:00:06,250 --> 01:00:10,050
Leave it to me. I'm good with Curling Bombs.

1390
01:00:10,850 --> 01:00:12,850
Can't do that one.

1391
01:00:12,850 --> 01:00:14,650
Couldn't pull that off.

1392
01:00:15,450 --> 01:00:17,390
Gonna mess them up with bombs.

1393
01:00:17,390 --> 01:00:19,250
Someone might be coming in. One person.

1394
01:00:21,520 --> 01:00:23,520
Fall back and ink.

1395
01:00:24,320 --> 01:00:29,390
Uh oh. Wait, maybe not. Actually maybe yes. Two of us are down.

1396
01:00:30,390 --> 01:00:34,190
Two in the center. Sorry. Got taken out by the Inkbrush.

1397
01:00:34,990 --> 01:00:36,990
Almost three of us are down.

1398
01:00:36,990 --> 01:00:39,990
What was that thing — that stick-like thing?

1399
01:00:39,990 --> 01:00:41,990
The straw-looking one?

1400
01:00:42,790 --> 01:00:44,790
Oh, the Megaphone Laser.

1401
01:00:44,790 --> 01:00:46,720
Megaphone Laser, yeah, Megaphone Laser!

1402
01:00:46,720 --> 01:00:48,590
Stop with the fireworks!

1403
01:00:49,390 --> 01:00:51,390
Fireworks~!

1404
01:00:52,620 --> 01:00:54,430
Whoa, seriously?!

1405
01:00:54,430 --> 01:00:56,220
Um, Pablo—

1406
01:00:56,220 --> 01:00:57,220
Got the middle!

1407
01:00:57,220 --> 01:00:58,220
Right or left?

1408
01:00:58,220 --> 01:00:59,020
Ah, they fell back.

1409
01:00:59,020 --> 01:01:00,980
Can't hit them?

1410
01:01:00,980 --> 01:01:01,820
Fireworks!

1411
01:01:01,820 --> 01:01:03,700
Oh no! Sorry!

1412
01:01:03,700 --> 01:01:04,860
Got taken out.

1413
01:01:04,860 --> 01:01:06,050
I forgive you.

1414
01:01:06,050 --> 01:01:07,240
Can't do it.

1415
01:01:07,240 --> 01:01:09,320
Forgiven, forgiven!

1416
01:01:09,320 --> 01:01:11,680
One of us is down.

1417
01:01:11,680 --> 01:01:13,440
We're not inking enough.

1418
01:01:13,440 --> 01:01:15,200
Yeah, let me climb up first and then go.

1419
01:01:15,200 --> 01:01:16,820
Ah, they climbed up.

1420
01:01:16,820 --> 01:01:19,140
They're climbing up.

1421
01:01:19,140 --> 01:01:24,900
Oh, they're causing chaos.

1422
01:01:24,900 --> 01:01:27,660
The center is gone.

1423
01:01:27,660 --> 01:01:29,620
Yeah.

1424
01:01:29,620 --> 01:01:31,150
So small!

1425
01:01:31,150 --> 01:01:32,140
What is this?

1426
01:01:32,140 --> 01:01:33,500
Nice?

1427
01:01:35,360 --> 01:01:36,690
Oh no! We lost the Rainmaker!

1428
01:01:36,690 --> 01:01:38,660
Sorry, the center is a mess.

1429
01:01:38,660 --> 01:01:40,460
Things are getting bad right now.

1430
01:01:43,620 --> 01:01:45,420
Hey, this is bad! What is this — this is probably really bad!

1431
01:01:45,420 --> 01:01:47,220
No wait, it's the King! That's it!

1432
01:01:49,220 --> 01:01:52,240
Probably!

1433
01:01:52,240 --> 01:01:53,240
Why?

1434
01:01:54,040 --> 01:01:56,040
We ended up trading.

1435
01:01:57,740 --> 01:01:59,240
Damn!

1436
01:02:00,040 --> 01:02:02,840
Go go go! Got the fireworks! Damn! Here we go!

1437
01:02:04,140 --> 01:02:06,740
Is it over? No, we still don't know!

1438
01:02:06,740 --> 01:02:10,740
Which way is this going?

1439
01:02:18,300 --> 01:02:25,220
This is pretty tough — when the center gets locked down it's super hard to break through.

1440
01:02:25,220 --> 01:02:28,020
Maybe I should switch to missiles. Yeah, good idea.

1441
01:02:34,010 --> 01:02:36,310
Should we fire missiles?

1442
01:02:36,310 --> 01:02:39,530
Or should I use the Ract that I'm terrible with?

1443
01:02:39,530 --> 01:02:40,530
Why?

1444
01:02:40,530 --> 01:02:43,370
The schedule changed!

1445
01:02:43,370 --> 01:02:46,530
Which means the stage is changing?

1446
01:02:46,530 --> 01:02:48,690
Fuu-tan takes the Ract,

1447
01:02:48,690 --> 01:02:50,170
covers everything in Cohock ink,

1448
01:02:50,170 --> 01:02:53,450
and becomes a missile-spamming machine!

1449
01:02:53,450 --> 01:02:54,490
Nice!

1450
01:02:54,490 --> 01:02:55,410
I see, I see.

1451
01:02:55,410 --> 01:02:56,370
OK OK, got it!

1452
01:02:56,370 --> 01:02:57,590
Where's next?

1453
01:02:57,590 --> 01:03:00,610
Kinme.

1454
01:03:00,610 --> 01:03:03,610
I can't tell just from the name.

1455
01:03:03,610 --> 01:03:05,210
It's the art museum!

1456
01:03:05,210 --> 01:03:06,210
The art museum?

1457
01:03:06,210 --> 01:03:08,210
Oh, that place with the spinning thing!

1458
01:03:08,210 --> 01:03:09,920
Yeah!

1459
01:03:09,920 --> 01:03:11,790
Oh, that place~

1460
01:03:11,790 --> 01:03:13,610
Waiting for a room~

1461
01:03:13,610 --> 01:03:14,610
Waiting~

1462
01:03:14,610 --> 01:03:16,610
I can wait~

1463
01:03:16,610 --> 01:03:18,610
Can we trust Fuu-tan to make the room?

1464
01:03:18,610 --> 01:03:19,610
I made it!

1465
01:03:19,610 --> 01:03:23,210
Fuu-tan, Fuu-tan, not yet, not yet~

1466
01:03:23,210 --> 01:03:25,210
Oh wait, hold on, no no, it's not ready yet!

1467
01:03:25,210 --> 01:03:27,010
Huh? Is it ready?

1468
01:03:27,010 --> 01:03:29,630
Careful, it just went into matchmaking, it's set now!

1469
01:03:29,630 --> 01:03:31,630
Careful, careful!

1470
01:03:31,630 --> 01:03:33,230
It's not ready!

1471
01:03:33,230 --> 01:03:37,030
I want to go to Fuu-tan's room!

1472
01:03:37,030 --> 01:03:38,830
A sleepover?

1473
01:03:38,830 --> 01:03:40,830
Don't say sleepover, sleepover~

1474
01:03:40,830 --> 01:03:42,630
You're welcome to come, you know!

1475
01:03:42,630 --> 01:03:44,430
I'll come!

1476
01:03:44,430 --> 01:03:46,430
But watch out for cat allergies.

1477
01:03:46,430 --> 01:03:47,340
Okay!

1478
01:03:47,340 --> 01:03:49,230
Kitties are so cute!

1479
01:03:49,230 --> 01:03:51,030
Kitty kitty~

1480
01:03:51,030 --> 01:03:52,830
Which one was it... this one?

1481
01:03:52,830 --> 01:03:54,630
Oh, no.

1482
01:03:54,630 --> 01:03:56,630
Everyone ended up with close-range weapons.

1483
01:03:58,430 --> 01:04:00,230
Impressively, everyone's close-range.

1484
01:04:00,230 --> 01:04:04,230
Maybe I should go with the Bamboozler's stats?

1485
01:04:06,530 --> 01:04:09,530
Wasn't the new Ract actually pretty good?

1486
01:04:10,330 --> 01:04:12,130
Oh really?

1487
01:04:12,130 --> 01:04:13,130
I have no idea.

1488
01:04:13,130 --> 01:04:14,130
Mote.

1489
01:04:16,390 --> 01:04:19,390
Hmm, what do you think about this?

1490
01:04:19,390 --> 01:04:21,390
Let me try this once.

1491
01:04:22,190 --> 01:04:22,990
I see.

1492
01:04:23,790 --> 01:04:28,150
Man, it's hard to decide~

1493
01:04:28,510 --> 01:04:33,830
But it's fun trying out all kinds of weapons! It is, right?

1494
01:04:33,830 --> 01:04:40,390
Swapping things around... maybe I'll try Momiji. Momiji's strong! Sounds good!

1495
01:04:40,390 --> 01:04:46,930
I don't really get what Torpedo does, but it's annoying to deal with. Yeah, Torpedo is super annoying.

1496
01:04:46,930 --> 01:04:54,630
Oh really? You know, there's the one where you shake it, and then there's the one with the homing function, right?

1497
01:04:54,630 --> 01:05:01,950
The non-shaking one? The shaking one is a bit of a hassle. Yeah, you have to shake it, so it's a pain.

1498
01:05:01,950 --> 01:05:10,630
Or the one that bounces around. Takes a bit of time though.

1499
01:05:10,630 --> 01:05:16,660
It just won't hit. This team's balance isn't great.

1500
01:05:16,660 --> 01:05:20,460
I think the balance is fine.

1501
01:05:20,460 --> 01:05:23,260
Like, in terms of voice and personality?

1502
01:05:23,260 --> 01:05:26,260
I'm talking about weapons.

1503
01:05:26,260 --> 01:05:31,560
Weapons.

1504
01:05:31,560 --> 01:05:34,560
Right, weapons.

1505
01:05:34,560 --> 01:05:37,360
Of course.

1506
01:05:37,360 --> 01:05:41,160
Personality?

1507
01:05:41,160 --> 01:05:43,160
The personality lineup is also great!

1508
01:05:43,160 --> 01:05:44,560
What do you mean?

1509
01:05:44,560 --> 01:05:46,060
Personality? Hmm...

1510
01:05:46,060 --> 01:05:48,360
Whoa! I think this might be my first time here!

1511
01:05:48,360 --> 01:05:49,360
Maybe my first time!

1512
01:05:49,360 --> 01:05:50,860
This stage is new!

1513
01:05:50,860 --> 01:05:52,560
A station?

1514
01:05:52,560 --> 01:05:53,160
Oh, a brush!

1515
01:05:53,160 --> 01:05:54,360
An airport! An airport!

1516
01:05:54,360 --> 01:05:56,360
It's an airport!

1517
01:05:56,360 --> 01:05:58,260
Yah! Yah! Yah!

1518
01:05:58,260 --> 01:06:00,460
Oh no! The brush is going wild!

1519
01:06:00,460 --> 01:06:03,660
Targeting the brush user is kind of a pain.

1520
01:06:03,660 --> 01:06:05,760
No way, I can't! Lend me your aim for a sec!

1521
01:06:05,760 --> 01:06:07,960
I'll lend my aim too!

1522
01:06:07,960 --> 01:06:10,960
Oh, nice!

1523
01:06:11,760 --> 01:06:14,760
Thank you, that helped!

1524
01:06:14,760 --> 01:06:16,760
I have no idea where I am on this map!

1525
01:06:16,760 --> 01:06:19,560
I'm not really a fan of this map

1526
01:06:20,560 --> 01:06:22,360
Oh no, I got hit by the Inkbrush!

1527
01:06:23,160 --> 01:06:25,160
Oh no! Something got me! What was that?!

1528
01:06:25,160 --> 01:06:27,160
It's a bucket! A bucket!

1529
01:06:27,160 --> 01:06:28,960
Isn't this stage way too big?

1530
01:06:28,960 --> 01:06:30,960
It is wide, like...

1531
01:06:30,960 --> 01:06:32,760
It's huge!

1532
01:06:33,600 --> 01:06:39,020
Whoa, that brush is crazy — they were behind me! The brush, the brush — got 'em! Nice! Nice!

1533
01:06:41,050 --> 01:06:45,210
So wide! Wide! Too wide!

1534
01:06:45,210 --> 01:06:52,290
This is too wide — only got one person

1535
01:06:52,290 --> 01:06:58,250
This is too wide, I can't even tell where the center is! Fired the missiles!

1536
01:06:58,250 --> 01:07:03,430
Got one with the missiles! Nice! Nice nice!

1537
01:07:03,430 --> 01:07:04,430
Got one with the Ract!

1538
01:07:04,430 --> 01:07:05,430
Nice!

1539
01:07:05,430 --> 01:07:06,430
Nice, Ract!

1540
01:07:08,030 --> 01:07:09,030
So this is the center!

1541
01:07:09,030 --> 01:07:10,030
They're hiding here!

1542
01:07:10,030 --> 01:07:11,030
They're there, they're there!

1543
01:07:11,830 --> 01:07:12,830
They're right here!

1544
01:07:13,630 --> 01:07:15,630
Got one but something got me!

1545
01:07:15,630 --> 01:07:17,430
Nice! It was a trade!

1546
01:07:17,430 --> 01:07:18,430
Well, maybe not exactly a trade

1547
01:07:19,230 --> 01:07:20,230
Pretty much a trade though

1548
01:07:20,230 --> 01:07:22,230
It was a trade, right? Yeah!

1549
01:07:23,030 --> 01:07:25,900
I see, there's a Ract on the left

1550
01:07:25,900 --> 01:07:26,830
Nice!

1551
01:07:26,830 --> 01:07:27,830
Nice, Ract!

1552
01:07:27,830 --> 01:07:28,830
Yikes!

1553
01:07:31,430 --> 01:07:32,660
Nice!

1554
01:07:32,660 --> 01:07:33,830
They're there again

1555
01:07:33,830 --> 01:07:35,030
Are there two brushes?

1556
01:07:35,030 --> 01:07:36,670
Nice!

1557
01:07:36,670 --> 01:07:38,670
I'll kill them with the Curling Bomb

1558
01:07:38,670 --> 01:07:39,470
Aw, couldn't get that one

1559
01:07:39,470 --> 01:07:40,670
Got one with the Dynamo!

1560
01:07:40,670 --> 01:07:42,970
Nice!

1561
01:07:42,970 --> 01:07:44,770
Going to mess up their side!

1562
01:07:44,770 --> 01:07:46,530
Fired the missiles!

1563
01:07:46,530 --> 01:07:49,790
Nice!

1564
01:07:49,790 --> 01:07:51,130
Over here—

1565
01:07:51,130 --> 01:07:51,930
Pablo's coming

1566
01:07:51,930 --> 01:07:54,590
Okay, got it!

1567
01:07:54,590 --> 01:07:59,650
Pablo's marked but they keep popping up everywhere

1568
01:07:59,650 --> 01:08:00,650
Hmm

1569
01:08:01,450 --> 01:08:02,450
Here we go

1570
01:08:03,800 --> 01:08:04,800
Here we go

1571
01:08:08,640 --> 01:08:09,440
No good

1572
01:08:09,440 --> 01:08:10,440
Nice!

1573
01:08:11,240 --> 01:08:13,040
Udon, udon, udon~

1574
01:08:14,340 --> 01:08:15,340
I want some udon

1575
01:08:15,340 --> 01:08:17,340
Oh, Ayuchi! Pablo and Ayuchi!

1576
01:08:17,340 --> 01:08:18,190
Nice!

1577
01:08:18,190 --> 01:08:19,140
Nice, Ayuchi!

1578
01:08:19,140 --> 01:08:20,140
We've basically taken out two of them

1579
01:08:20,140 --> 01:08:21,140
Okay

1580
01:08:21,140 --> 01:08:22,940
I'm scared of where Pablo might be

1581
01:08:22,940 --> 01:08:23,940
Oh, over there

1582
01:08:24,740 --> 01:08:26,670
Ract on the left

1583
01:08:26,670 --> 01:08:27,540
Okay

1584
01:08:28,340 --> 01:08:30,140
Bucket, bam!

1585
01:08:30,140 --> 01:08:31,940
Oh sorry, I went down with them

1586
01:08:31,940 --> 01:08:33,940
Went down together with the last one

1587
01:08:36,750 --> 01:08:39,550
We might still have a chance though! Let's keep trying!

1588
01:08:39,550 --> 01:08:41,350
This is going in

1589
01:08:41,350 --> 01:08:42,350
How's it looking?

1590
01:08:42,350 --> 01:08:43,350
We might actually have a chance here

1591
01:08:43,350 --> 01:08:44,350
I wasn't watching the back

1592
01:08:44,350 --> 01:08:45,350
We might have made it

1593
01:08:45,350 --> 01:08:47,150
Did we?

1594
01:08:47,150 --> 01:08:48,150
I think we got it?

1595
01:08:48,150 --> 01:08:49,150
We got it, right?

1596
01:08:49,150 --> 01:08:50,150
Yeah, I think we got it

1597
01:08:50,150 --> 01:08:51,150
I'm pretty sure we got it

1598
01:08:51,150 --> 01:08:53,990
Oh thank goodness!

1599
01:08:53,990 --> 01:08:55,990
We finally won!

1600
01:08:55,990 --> 01:08:56,790
We finally won!

1601
01:08:56,790 --> 01:08:58,590
Yay!

1602
01:08:58,590 --> 01:09:00,390
We did it, we did it!

1603
01:09:00,390 --> 01:09:02,190
First win?

1604
01:09:02,190 --> 01:09:04,190
First win! First win!

1605
01:09:04,190 --> 01:09:06,190
First win after a whole hour, that's rough!

1606
01:09:06,190 --> 01:09:08,190
First win, that's crazy!

1607
01:09:08,190 --> 01:09:10,190
Let's go!

1608
01:09:10,190 --> 01:09:12,190
Come down to our level!

1609
01:09:12,190 --> 01:09:13,990
Yay!

1610
01:09:13,990 --> 01:09:15,790
Thank goodness!

1611
01:09:15,790 --> 01:09:17,790
Nice, nice!

1612
01:09:17,790 --> 01:09:19,590
It really is fun though.

1613
01:09:19,590 --> 01:09:21,590
Splatoon as a game...

1614
01:09:21,590 --> 01:09:23,590
It's so fun!

1615
01:09:23,590 --> 01:09:25,390
The moment you win—

1616
01:09:26,390 --> 01:09:28,190
So fun, so fun!

1617
01:09:28,190 --> 01:09:29,990
That was great!

1618
01:09:29,990 --> 01:09:31,790
Great, great!

1619
01:09:34,020 --> 01:09:35,020
I'll use it.

1620
01:09:35,020 --> 01:09:36,820
Go for it!

1621
01:09:36,820 --> 01:09:38,620
The bow?

1622
01:09:38,620 --> 01:09:40,420
Being able to use the bow is impressive!

1623
01:09:40,420 --> 01:09:42,220
That bow is seriously impossible for me.

1624
01:09:42,220 --> 01:09:44,220
Being able to use the bow is amazing.

1625
01:09:44,220 --> 01:09:47,220
But whether I can use it or not, it's still fun!

1626
01:09:47,220 --> 01:09:49,020
The curved shots are seriously hard.

1627
01:09:49,820 --> 01:09:52,820
Landing curved shots looks so cool though.

1628
01:09:52,820 --> 01:09:54,820
It's cool, it's cool, but still...

1629
01:09:54,820 --> 01:09:56,820
It's cool, so being able to do it is impressive.

1630
01:09:56,820 --> 01:09:58,820
10x!

1631
01:09:58,820 --> 01:10:00,420
10x!

1632
01:10:00,420 --> 01:10:02,220
10x match!

1633
01:10:02,220 --> 01:10:04,020
10x!

1634
01:10:04,020 --> 01:10:06,020
10x!

1635
01:10:06,020 --> 01:10:07,820
10x!

1636
01:10:07,820 --> 01:10:09,820
10x points!

1637
01:10:09,820 --> 01:10:11,620
10x points is huge, that's huge!

1638
01:10:11,620 --> 01:10:13,620
Ugh, no...

1639
01:10:13,620 --> 01:10:15,620
That's a rough team comp.

1640
01:10:15,620 --> 01:10:17,620
It's a heavy comp.

1641
01:10:17,620 --> 01:10:19,620
It's heavy, huh.

1642
01:10:20,940 --> 01:10:23,740
The Splatana Wiper is strong, you know.

1643
01:10:23,740 --> 01:10:25,540
Oh really?

1644
01:10:26,400 --> 01:10:28,200
My ink isn't refilling though.

1645
01:10:29,000 --> 01:10:30,800
It's hard to use.

1646
01:10:31,260 --> 01:10:35,260
The Splatana Wiper — Wipers in general are hard to use.

1647
01:10:37,560 --> 01:10:39,360
I wasted my Trizooka.

1648
01:10:39,360 --> 01:10:41,160
Firing missiles~!

1649
01:10:41,160 --> 01:10:43,160
Got one Splatana Wiper! Nice!

1650
01:10:43,580 --> 01:10:45,380
There's always someone up top.

1651
01:10:46,300 --> 01:10:50,830
Ugh, I keep getting shot at!

1652
01:10:50,830 --> 01:10:52,000
And a Fluiddrive too—

1653
01:10:52,000 --> 01:10:54,620
Oh, Inkjet!

1654
01:10:54,620 --> 01:10:56,220
No no no no!

1655
01:10:56,220 --> 01:10:57,840
Nice, nice!

1656
01:10:57,840 --> 01:11:00,260
Fluiddrive V.

1657
01:11:00,260 --> 01:11:01,420
What even is Fluiddrive V?

1658
01:11:01,420 --> 01:11:05,100
What's Fluiddrive V?

1659
01:11:05,100 --> 01:11:06,040
I don't know it.

1660
01:11:06,040 --> 01:11:07,040
I don't know it either.

1661
01:11:07,040 --> 01:11:08,280
No idea.

1662
01:11:08,280 --> 01:11:10,700
No idea what Fluiddrive V is.

1663
01:11:10,700 --> 01:11:11,900
What is that, what is that?

1664
01:11:11,900 --> 01:11:12,360
Whoa.

1665
01:11:12,360 --> 01:11:13,620
That's Fluiddrive V.

1666
01:11:13,620 --> 01:11:14,180
Probably.

1667
01:11:14,180 --> 01:11:15,180
Seriously?

1668
01:11:16,200 --> 01:11:18,030
Probably. Fluiddrive gets you all wet, you know.

1669
01:11:18,220 --> 01:11:20,220
I see it sometimes. Not sure though.

1670
01:11:20,860 --> 01:11:22,860
Fluiddrive V is actually pretty strong.

1671
01:11:23,720 --> 01:11:25,720
Ugh, Fluiddrive V.

1672
01:11:26,340 --> 01:11:27,340
So much.

1673
01:11:31,080 --> 01:11:31,980
Damn.

1674
01:11:33,840 --> 01:11:34,840
It's raining!

1675
01:11:36,280 --> 01:11:37,080
Oh no, this is bad!

1676
01:11:37,080 --> 01:11:41,790
The Splatana Wiper got me. Maybe there's no more Wiper.

1677
01:11:41,790 --> 01:11:43,300
No wait, there's another one.

1678
01:11:43,300 --> 01:11:46,080
Yikes! Too close! I think we traded!

1679
01:11:46,080 --> 01:11:47,420
Nice~ Nice~

1680
01:11:50,470 --> 01:11:53,630
Firing Tenta Missiles~! Oh, I could only target one person.

1681
01:11:53,630 --> 01:11:55,470
It's fine, it's fine! Nice~

1682
01:11:55,470 --> 01:11:57,430
Nice Marmi~

1683
01:12:01,860 --> 01:12:03,180
Got a Zipcaster! Where are they?

1684
01:12:03,180 --> 01:12:04,800
Firing missiles~! Show me the Zipcaster!

1685
01:12:04,800 --> 01:12:06,800
Ahh~ the Zipcaster—

1686
01:12:08,870 --> 01:12:10,800
They keep targeting this spot, huh

1687
01:12:10,990 --> 01:12:12,790
We want to take the middle

1688
01:12:12,790 --> 01:12:14,290
We want the middle

1689
01:12:14,290 --> 01:12:16,130
I'm at least disrupting the middle right now!

1690
01:12:16,130 --> 01:12:18,130
This rain is the worst!

1691
01:12:18,130 --> 01:12:20,260
It's a good fight! It's a good fight!

1692
01:12:20,260 --> 01:12:22,220
Fall back! Retreating for now!

1693
01:12:22,220 --> 01:12:23,860
Okay

1694
01:12:23,860 --> 01:12:25,860
Ugh, I hate this rain

1695
01:12:25,860 --> 01:12:27,860
Their bow is so annoying

1696
01:12:27,860 --> 01:12:30,160
No way!

1697
01:12:30,160 --> 01:12:32,200
Couldn't get them!

1698
01:12:32,200 --> 01:12:34,780
Dualies Squelcher

1699
01:12:34,780 --> 01:12:36,780
There's no point fighting a bow with a bow

1700
01:12:36,780 --> 01:12:39,240
Whoa!

1701
01:12:39,240 --> 01:12:41,240
Not the LZ!

1702
01:12:41,240 --> 01:12:43,240
Got someone!

1703
01:12:43,240 --> 01:12:45,240
Oh no! They're breaking through the middle!

1704
01:12:45,240 --> 01:12:46,920
This is bad, this is bad

1705
01:12:46,920 --> 01:12:49,390
They're coming in

1706
01:12:49,390 --> 01:12:50,420
Got them! Got them!

1707
01:12:50,420 --> 01:12:50,760
Nice

1708
01:12:50,760 --> 01:12:53,520
We got them, but...

1709
01:12:53,520 --> 01:12:56,800
We need to re-ink

1710
01:12:56,800 --> 01:13:00,280
This is bad, bad, bad

1711
01:13:00,280 --> 01:13:01,500
You were there the whole time?!

1712
01:13:01,500 --> 01:13:03,360
There's a roller hiding

1713
01:13:03,360 --> 01:13:04,060
Seriously

1714
01:13:04,060 --> 01:13:07,480
This is bad

1715
01:13:07,480 --> 01:13:10,600
Just let me climb up

1716
01:13:10,600 --> 01:13:12,140
No good

1717
01:13:12,140 --> 01:13:15,080
Aww, everyone did their best though

1718
01:13:15,080 --> 01:13:19,300
Before it ends—

1719
01:13:19,300 --> 01:13:20,800
Everyone really did their best

1720
01:13:20,800 --> 01:13:22,140
We did our best

1721
01:13:22,140 --> 01:13:23,720
We gave it our all

1722
01:13:23,720 --> 01:13:25,960
Everyone was really trying hard

1723
01:13:25,960 --> 01:13:26,920
It just didn't work out

1724
01:13:26,920 --> 01:13:30,180
Everyone did great

1725
01:13:30,180 --> 01:13:31,380
It's a weapon matchup thing

1726
01:13:31,380 --> 01:13:33,300
On to the next one

1727
01:13:33,300 --> 01:13:34,520
I mean, you know

1728
01:13:34,520 --> 01:13:35,580
Mio-sha's corner—

1729
01:13:35,580 --> 01:13:38,140
It's your first time at this airport stage, right

1730
01:13:38,140 --> 01:13:39,780
No, it's my second time

1731
01:13:39,780 --> 01:13:44,500
Don't point that out, don't point it out

1732
01:13:44,500 --> 01:13:48,880
It's my second time, but I still haven't seen all of it

1733
01:13:48,880 --> 01:13:51,580
You haven't seen the other side yet, right?

1734
01:13:51,580 --> 01:13:52,680
Yeah, yeah, yeah, exactly

1735
01:13:52,680 --> 01:13:53,740
Right, Mio-sha?

1736
01:13:53,740 --> 01:13:55,180
We'll get there, we'll get there

1737
01:13:55,180 --> 01:13:56,620
Well, well, well

1738
01:13:56,620 --> 01:13:58,200
Yeah, that's true

1739
01:13:58,200 --> 01:14:02,440
After like 5 or 6 more matches you'll probably get used to it

1740
01:14:02,440 --> 01:14:03,480
You think so?

1741
01:14:03,480 --> 01:14:04,560
Yeah, right?

1742
01:14:04,560 --> 01:14:05,020
Yeah, for sure

1743
01:14:05,020 --> 01:14:06,600
Right?

1744
01:14:06,600 --> 01:14:07,040
Yeah

1745
01:14:07,040 --> 01:14:08,840
Right?

1746
01:14:08,840 --> 01:14:13,700
Oh nice, Carbonara and Bolognese — that's a good combo

1747
01:14:13,700 --> 01:14:18,300
They change their names to food names periodically, right

1748
01:14:18,300 --> 01:14:20,380
What did they use before?

1749
01:14:20,380 --> 01:14:22,900
Wasn't it shiitake and something?

1750
01:14:22,900 --> 01:14:26,640
What was it... shiitake and shimeji, wasn't it?

1751
01:14:26,640 --> 01:14:27,500
That's cute

1752
01:14:27,500 --> 01:14:30,320
But Cavalier too—

1753
01:14:30,320 --> 01:14:32,860
At a glance it kind of looks like it matches, right?

1754
01:14:32,860 --> 01:14:34,680
True, it's all katakana

1755
01:14:34,680 --> 01:14:37,420
True. Passed, passed

1756
01:14:37,420 --> 01:14:38,680
Dog...

1757
01:14:42,280 --> 01:14:43,280
Airport again?

1758
01:14:43,280 --> 01:14:46,080
It's Kinmedai! Kinmedai! Kinmedai!

1759
01:14:46,880 --> 01:14:47,880
Nostalgic

1760
01:14:47,880 --> 01:14:50,880
It's nostalgic, right? Kinmedai... I really can't deal with it

1761
01:14:52,680 --> 01:14:54,680
It's really impossible, like, I just can't.

1762
01:14:54,680 --> 01:14:57,680
Feeling all nostalgic and still can't handle it.

1763
01:14:58,480 --> 01:15:02,480
When I was really deep into Splatoon, this felt like a stage that came up a lot.

1764
01:15:02,480 --> 01:15:04,540
Yeah, that's actually true.

1765
01:15:04,540 --> 01:15:05,550
Ahh.

1766
01:15:05,550 --> 01:15:08,620
Like a museum, or a university, or an art gallery vibe.

1767
01:15:08,620 --> 01:15:10,870
Yeah, yeah.

1768
01:15:12,880 --> 01:15:14,200
That's the kind of image it gives off.

1769
01:15:14,200 --> 01:15:15,280
Valmi!

1770
01:15:15,280 --> 01:15:17,080
I'm shooting Valmi!

1771
01:15:17,080 --> 01:15:19,040
Got taken out by a Goshichi-Nana, on the right.

1772
01:15:19,040 --> 01:15:20,200
Okay!

1773
01:15:20,200 --> 01:15:21,540
Two are down right now.

1774
01:15:21,540 --> 01:15:22,500
Got one!

1775
01:15:22,500 --> 01:15:24,640
They're down.

1776
01:15:24,640 --> 01:15:26,640
You know, in FPS games—

1777
01:15:26,640 --> 01:15:30,140
I always wonder why people count kills as "one sheet, two sheets."

1778
01:15:30,140 --> 01:15:32,300
Isn't it how you count squids?

1779
01:15:32,300 --> 01:15:36,240
But don't FPS players say "one, two" like that pretty often?

1780
01:15:36,240 --> 01:15:39,060
Sometimes it just comes out that way even without thinking.

1781
01:15:39,060 --> 01:15:42,930
"One person, two people." Maybe "hitori, futari" is too tiring to say?

1782
01:15:42,930 --> 01:15:47,840
"Ichimai, ichimai." "Ichimai" has a kind of... "mai" sound to it.

1783
01:15:47,840 --> 01:15:49,840
The number of characters is the same though.

1784
01:15:49,840 --> 01:15:52,640
It's like... "mai." Just "mai."

1785
01:15:52,640 --> 01:15:57,640
"Hitori, hitori." "Mai-mai." "Mai-mai." See, "mai" is probably easier, right?

1786
01:15:57,640 --> 01:15:58,640
"Mai-mai."

1787
01:15:58,640 --> 01:16:00,640
It's about ease of saying it, ease of saying it.

1788
01:16:00,640 --> 01:16:02,440
Oh no!

1789
01:16:02,440 --> 01:16:04,240
Nice, nice!

1790
01:16:04,240 --> 01:16:06,040
Nice?

1791
01:16:06,040 --> 01:16:08,040
Oh no, I got taken out!

1792
01:16:08,040 --> 01:16:09,840
Ugh, the Tenta Missiles are in the way!

1793
01:16:09,840 --> 01:16:11,730
Tenta Missiles!

1794
01:16:11,730 --> 01:16:13,440
Okay!

1795
01:16:13,440 --> 01:16:15,240
Only to the right—

1796
01:16:15,240 --> 01:16:17,040
Oh, got one!

1797
01:16:17,040 --> 01:16:18,840
Nice, nice, nice!

1798
01:16:18,840 --> 01:16:20,840
Ah, I can't get that one.

1799
01:16:20,840 --> 01:16:22,840
I was trying to go wild just once—

1800
01:16:22,840 --> 01:16:26,740
I tried but—

1801
01:16:26,740 --> 01:16:28,540
Couldn't do it.

1802
01:16:28,540 --> 01:16:29,760
Couldn't do it.

1803
01:16:29,760 --> 01:16:30,640
Oh no, oh no, oh no!

1804
01:16:30,640 --> 01:16:32,340
There was one more!

1805
01:16:32,340 --> 01:16:33,480
Oh no, I got taken out!

1806
01:16:33,480 --> 01:16:34,940
Two of them are down on the enemy side.

1807
01:16:34,940 --> 01:16:36,840
Okay!

1808
01:16:36,840 --> 01:16:38,700
Woo-hoo!

1809
01:16:38,700 --> 01:16:40,340
Now's the time to push!

1810
01:16:40,340 --> 01:16:42,460
Now's the time to push!

1811
01:16:42,460 --> 01:16:44,280
Firing the Booyah Bomb!

1812
01:16:44,280 --> 01:16:45,220
Nice!

1813
01:16:45,220 --> 01:16:46,260
Ink runs out so fast.

1814
01:16:46,260 --> 01:16:46,960
Ugh!

1815
01:16:46,960 --> 01:16:48,400
Just three left, three!

1816
01:16:48,400 --> 01:16:49,500
Oh, nice!

1817
01:16:49,500 --> 01:16:51,200
Sorry, sorry, someone's coming from the right!

1818
01:16:51,200 --> 01:16:53,520
Left? Which way — left or front?

1819
01:16:53,520 --> 01:16:55,440
Glasses guy, glasses guy, there's a glasses guy!

1820
01:16:55,440 --> 01:16:56,300
Got him!

1821
01:16:56,300 --> 01:16:56,800
Nice!

1822
01:16:56,800 --> 01:16:58,800
There was a Gal there, in that spot.

1823
01:17:00,720 --> 01:17:02,700
Watch out! Landing!

1824
01:17:03,160 --> 01:17:05,160
Ugh, landing hurts.

1825
01:17:05,820 --> 01:17:07,620
Ah, couldn't get them.

1826
01:17:09,060 --> 01:17:12,360
Hey! My aim is completely off!

1827
01:17:12,360 --> 01:17:13,980
There's a Pablo coming this way!

1828
01:17:13,980 --> 01:17:14,540
Oh, nice?

1829
01:17:14,540 --> 01:17:15,240
Nice.

1830
01:17:15,240 --> 01:17:16,160
Okay, that was rough.

1831
01:17:16,160 --> 01:17:18,000
No, that's not an Explosher!

1832
01:17:18,300 --> 01:17:19,980
Okay, that's annoying, I want to deal with it.

1833
01:17:19,980 --> 01:17:20,900
Yes, got it!

1834
01:17:20,900 --> 01:17:21,900
Nice! Nice!

1835
01:17:21,900 --> 01:17:23,740
I've got it right now!

1836
01:17:24,300 --> 01:17:26,800
One down! Oh no, oh no, oh no!

1837
01:17:28,390 --> 01:17:33,180
Are they there? Ugh, I was one shot away! They're getting in!

1838
01:17:33,180 --> 01:17:37,990
Okay! Stop, stop, stop — cut that out, cut it out, cut it out!

1839
01:17:40,750 --> 01:17:43,550
Ugh, use your special already!

1840
01:17:43,550 --> 01:17:48,200
Just go away already!

1841
01:17:53,600 --> 01:17:57,400
Serious! What? Cusion might be amazing!

1842
01:17:57,400 --> 01:18:01,400
Cusion is amazing! Only Cusion!

1843
01:18:01,730 --> 01:18:07,280
Nah, in Goldfish it's all about mobility — whoever has it wins. Oh, really?

1844
01:18:07,280 --> 01:18:17,280
Yeah, right? The ones who can rush in and flank are strong. Like, Pablo is strong, huh? Pablo is strong, for sure. Pablo...

1845
01:18:17,540 --> 01:18:19,900
Ah, don't look, don't look!

1846
01:18:19,900 --> 01:18:29,020
Everyone don't look at this. But saying "don't look" means look, right? No no, if I say don't look then you really can't look, you can't look!

1847
01:18:29,020 --> 01:18:39,020
You can't look! Oh no, you couldn't look~ I see. Well then. You're gonna look anyway~ Don't say "well then." Stop it. Well then, Cavalier— Cavalier—

1848
01:18:41,810 --> 01:18:51,810
Hmm, they're probably getting a ton of kills... and they're not even watching, but then if you comment about it, aren't you watching while snacking? That makes you a watcher!

1849
01:18:59,810 --> 01:19:02,730
Here we go!

1850
01:19:02,730 --> 01:19:05,710
It's either they're getting a ton of kills or getting killed a ton — one of the two.

1851
01:19:05,710 --> 01:19:06,870
True, true.

1852
01:19:06,870 --> 01:19:11,550
So you're saying don't look even if you're getting kills?

1853
01:19:12,950 --> 01:19:13,310
Yeah.

1854
01:19:13,310 --> 01:19:15,490
On the flip side, if you say don't look, don't look—

1855
01:19:15,490 --> 01:19:17,230
You're actually getting a ton of kills!

1856
01:19:17,230 --> 01:19:18,050
Ah, so that's it.

1857
01:19:18,050 --> 01:19:20,450
Honestly I was just getting wrecked the whole time.

1858
01:19:20,450 --> 01:19:24,830
Using reverse psychology on people who want to look when told not to.

1859
01:19:24,830 --> 01:19:26,390
I see, I see.

1860
01:19:26,390 --> 01:19:28,160
So it was that?

1861
01:19:28,360 --> 01:19:28,880
Oh, watch out!

1862
01:19:28,880 --> 01:19:29,840
Ugh!

1863
01:19:29,840 --> 01:19:30,860
Heavy!

1864
01:19:30,860 --> 01:19:31,860
Ugh, ugh!

1865
01:19:31,860 --> 01:19:33,260
Ugh!

1866
01:19:33,260 --> 01:19:36,660
The Moji Shooter is dangerous! Please take it out!

1867
01:19:36,660 --> 01:19:37,660
Is it dangerous?

1868
01:19:37,660 --> 01:19:38,860
It's dangerous! Please take it out!

1869
01:19:38,860 --> 01:19:39,960
It's dangerous!

1870
01:19:39,960 --> 01:19:41,540
Looks like we'll trade, on our end.

1871
01:19:41,540 --> 01:19:42,760
Going for Trizooka!

1872
01:19:42,760 --> 01:19:43,260
Got it!

1873
01:19:43,260 --> 01:19:44,290
Turtle is out.

1874
01:19:44,290 --> 01:19:44,900
Yep.

1875
01:19:44,900 --> 01:19:45,960
Stingray is out too.

1876
01:19:45,960 --> 01:19:46,860
Yep.

1877
01:19:47,360 --> 01:19:48,660
Wait, two specials out?

1878
01:19:49,760 --> 01:19:51,560
Are they really? Are they?

1879
01:19:51,560 --> 01:19:52,760
They're not.

1880
01:19:52,760 --> 01:19:54,360
Oh, I traded with someone.

1881
01:19:54,360 --> 01:19:54,860
Nice, nice!

1882
01:19:54,860 --> 01:19:56,860
A Splat Bomb is being thrown in.

1883
01:19:56,860 --> 01:19:58,660
Nice, got one!

1884
01:19:58,660 --> 01:20:00,460
Nice, got one!

1885
01:20:05,480 --> 01:20:07,480
Should we go for the middle?

1886
01:20:07,480 --> 01:20:09,760
Careful.

1887
01:20:09,760 --> 01:20:11,610
Firing missiles!

1888
01:20:11,610 --> 01:20:13,410
Wait, hold on.

1889
01:20:13,410 --> 01:20:15,210
Don't spread out.

1890
01:20:15,210 --> 01:20:17,210
Nice!

1891
