02:05:31,040 --> 02:05:32,180
Yeah.

2948
02:05:32,180 --> 02:05:34,660
Did they break through at all?

2949
02:05:34,660 --> 02:05:36,740
No, I think we're still fine.

2950
02:05:36,740 --> 02:05:39,900
Oh, they're inking the center though.

2951
02:05:39,900 --> 02:05:40,360
No way!

2952
02:05:40,360 --> 02:05:44,110
Well, I think we've got it though.

2953
02:05:44,110 --> 02:05:45,390
Yeah, I think we pulled it off.

2954
02:05:45,390 --> 02:05:46,270
Somehow.

2955
02:05:46,270 --> 02:05:49,670
Flare and the others really disrupted them.

2956
02:05:49,670 --> 02:05:51,310
You're right!

2957
02:05:51,310 --> 02:05:52,230
That was intense!

2958
02:05:52,230 --> 02:05:55,110
That charger was getting bullied out there.

2959
02:05:55,110 --> 02:06:00,050
Two chargers on the same team does tend to cause problems.

2960
02:06:00,050 --> 02:06:01,850
Yeah, for sure.

2961
02:06:01,850 --> 02:06:02,850
Nice!

2962
02:06:02,850 --> 02:06:04,850
They had quite a few people set up there

2963
02:06:04,850 --> 02:06:05,650
Nice, nice!

2964
02:06:05,650 --> 02:06:08,880
Nice defense!

2965
02:06:08,880 --> 02:06:12,480
If only this had been a 100x battle...

2966
02:06:12,480 --> 02:06:14,480
This is so fun!

2967
02:06:14,480 --> 02:06:18,280
Can we make it retroactive?

2968
02:06:18,280 --> 02:06:19,280
That's a bit much

2969
02:06:19,280 --> 02:06:20,280
Can't we just call it a 100x?

2970
02:06:20,280 --> 02:06:21,280
Can we?

2971
02:06:21,280 --> 02:06:23,280
That might be a little too convenient

2972
02:06:23,280 --> 02:06:24,280
No good?

2973
02:06:24,280 --> 02:06:25,280
Pretty convenient though

2974
02:06:25,280 --> 02:06:26,280
No good?

2975
02:06:26,280 --> 02:06:29,140
The moment I realized it was a 100x, my hands started sweating like crazy

2976
02:06:29,140 --> 02:06:30,440
Right, same!

2977
02:06:30,440 --> 02:06:32,560
And then you mess up

2978
02:06:32,560 --> 02:06:33,680
That's so true

2979
02:06:33,680 --> 02:06:35,780
Alright, let's go for a 333x then

2980
02:06:35,780 --> 02:06:39,900
I want it! I really want it!

2981
02:06:39,900 --> 02:06:43,300
I feel like I've only gotten a 333x once myself

2982
02:06:43,300 --> 02:06:44,100
Oh really?

2983
02:06:44,100 --> 02:06:45,420
I've had it like twice, twice

2984
02:06:45,420 --> 02:06:47,200
Was it twice?

2985
02:06:47,200 --> 02:06:49,240
Like, Flare and IRyS are already just assumed to be playing together

2986
02:06:49,240 --> 02:06:51,620
It's kind of cute how that's just a given now

2987
02:06:51,620 --> 02:07:01,120
IRyS was like, if I can't play with them today, I'm not doing it — something like that. Oh really? Wow, she said that? That's amazing.

2988
02:07:01,120 --> 02:07:05,020
That's so sweet. So cute. Yeah.

2989
02:07:05,020 --> 02:07:13,820
Splatoon is just more fun together, right? Totally. Playing alone you start to feel a certain way after a while.

2990
02:07:13,820 --> 02:07:18,560
Makes sense. OK. Looks like I'm on painting duty here.

2991
02:07:18,560 --> 02:07:23,390
I'll ink as I go, when I have the chance.

2992
02:07:26,580 --> 02:07:27,580
Watch out for the Dynamo.

2993
02:07:27,580 --> 02:07:29,580
Stop it, stop it!

2994
02:07:30,380 --> 02:07:31,380
I wanna use the Roller too.

2995
02:07:31,380 --> 02:07:33,380
Megaphone Laser!

2996
02:07:34,180 --> 02:07:35,180
Got hit by the Megaphone.

2997
02:07:35,180 --> 02:07:37,180
Got me.

2998
02:07:40,340 --> 02:07:42,340
Make sure to ink all the way into the corners.

2999
02:07:42,340 --> 02:07:45,340
Inking all the way into the corners is actually really important.

3000
02:07:47,140 --> 02:07:48,140
Oh no, oh no, oh no!

3001
02:07:48,940 --> 02:07:51,440
Ugh, I was just about to do that

3002
02:07:53,250 --> 02:07:54,750
Ah, they spotted me

3003
02:07:57,000 --> 02:07:58,500
Ah, got splatted!

3004
02:07:58,800 --> 02:07:59,800
Who's this?

3005
02:08:01,100 --> 02:08:02,600
Pro Modeler RG

3006
02:08:09,660 --> 02:08:11,160
Stop it, stop it, stop it!

3007
02:08:11,960 --> 02:08:13,460
Stop it! The laser!

3008
02:08:15,760 --> 02:08:18,260
Stop it! Ink management, stop it! Stop it!

3009
02:08:19,560 --> 02:08:20,560
Please, please

3010
02:08:23,110 --> 02:08:26,910
Nice! But wait, they already used their drink so it'll run out fast

3011
02:08:26,910 --> 02:08:31,270
OK wait, they're not even getting to drink it

3012
02:08:31,270 --> 02:08:35,070
We just barely won — oh no! Got splatted!

3013
02:08:35,070 --> 02:08:38,710
Nice

3014
02:08:39,710 --> 02:08:44,510
Ugh, I've just been wandering around this area — I want to push up a bit more

3015
02:08:48,100 --> 02:08:50,900
Oh no no no!

3016
02:08:50,900 --> 02:08:53,900
Dynamo! Dynamo, you!

3017
02:08:53,900 --> 02:08:55,900
That aim is so good!

3018
02:08:57,700 --> 02:08:59,810
That Dynamo player is good

3019
02:09:00,810 --> 02:09:01,810
Skilled Dynamo

3020
02:09:02,610 --> 02:09:03,610
What a skilled Dynamo

3021
02:09:03,610 --> 02:09:05,410
Quite the skilled Dynamo we have here

3022
02:09:05,410 --> 02:09:06,410
The matchup is rough

3023
02:09:07,210 --> 02:09:09,210
I wish they'd stop with the laser

3024
02:09:11,320 --> 02:09:12,120
Laser over here too

3025
02:09:12,120 --> 02:09:13,920
I hate it

3026
02:09:14,720 --> 02:09:15,720
Weird, right?

3027
02:09:15,720 --> 02:09:17,520
Got them! Took out the Dynamo!

3028
02:09:17,520 --> 02:09:21,120
The Dynamo is insane! There's another one! There's another Dynamo?!

3029
02:09:20,920 --> 02:09:22,420
Isn't that a Carbon? Carbon

3030
02:09:22,420 --> 02:09:24,020
Oh, it's a Carbon

3031
02:09:24,020 --> 02:09:25,420
Something's dying over there

3032
02:09:25,420 --> 02:09:27,720
Fireworks! Bombs everywhere!

3033
02:09:27,720 --> 02:09:30,720
Yeah, Curling Bombs really work on Dynamo players

3034
02:09:30,720 --> 02:09:31,420
Makes sense

3035
02:09:31,420 --> 02:09:32,420
Oh, it works, it works, it works!

3036
02:09:32,420 --> 02:09:34,920
You want to place them under the Dynamo when they're jumping

3037
02:09:34,920 --> 02:09:36,920
Right, right, right

3038
02:09:36,920 --> 02:09:38,220
No bombs left

3039
02:09:38,220 --> 02:09:40,220
Easy target — they're practically a free kill

3040
02:09:40,220 --> 02:09:40,820
Man...

3041
02:09:40,820 --> 02:09:41,720
A sitting duck

3042
02:09:41,720 --> 02:09:43,720
We're sitting ducks for Splash Bombs

3043
02:09:45,690 --> 02:09:48,390
Yes yes yes yes! Nice nice nice! Nice job! Nice job!

3044
02:09:48,390 --> 02:09:50,390
Oh no oh no oh no! Nice!

3045
02:09:50,690 --> 02:09:53,190
Fall! Fall already! Fall already! Nice!

3046
02:09:52,990 --> 02:09:53,490
Go! Go!

3047
02:09:53,190 --> 02:09:54,990
Go go go!

3048
02:09:54,990 --> 02:09:56,830
I'm gonna fly off!

3049
02:09:56,830 --> 02:09:58,630
Fireworks!

3050
02:09:58,630 --> 02:10:00,560
Use the fireworks! Everyone use the fireworks!

3051
02:10:00,560 --> 02:10:02,430
Okay~

3052
02:10:02,430 --> 02:10:05,240
Sorry!

3053
02:10:05,240 --> 02:10:06,840
Oh no, this is bad!

3054
02:10:06,840 --> 02:10:08,840
It's a Carbon! This is bad!

3055
02:10:08,840 --> 02:10:10,840
Which is it?!

3056
02:10:10,840 --> 02:10:12,840
Those are complete opposites in weight

3057
02:10:12,840 --> 02:10:14,840
This is bad! This is bad! Carbon! Which one is it?!

3058
02:10:14,840 --> 02:10:16,640
Which one is this?!

3059
02:10:16,640 --> 02:10:18,440
Hmm, how about this?

3060
02:10:18,440 --> 02:10:25,290
Nice!

3061
02:10:25,290 --> 02:10:30,290
I got three gold medals for the first time in a while. Someone fist bump me.

3062
02:10:30,290 --> 02:10:38,610
We did it. Koro and Mio.

3063
02:10:38,610 --> 02:10:43,210
There was one silver too. Should we swap back?

3064
02:10:43,210 --> 02:10:45,980
Got to fist bump for the first time in a while.

3065
02:10:45,980 --> 02:10:47,810
OK

3066
02:10:49,610 --> 02:10:51,610
I wanna fist bump~

3067
02:10:51,610 --> 02:10:53,610
Let's fist bump!

3068
02:10:55,410 --> 02:10:57,410
Maybe I'll try the bath stage~

3069
02:10:57,410 --> 02:10:59,220
Betting that Kinmedai is coming next

3070
02:11:01,210 --> 02:11:03,210
Betting that Kinmedai is coming

3071
02:11:03,210 --> 02:11:05,210
It'd be nice if it came~

3072
02:11:05,210 --> 02:11:07,210
That means it'll be Ryuguu Terminal then

3073
02:11:07,210 --> 02:11:09,210
You think so~?

3074
02:11:09,210 --> 02:11:11,210
Shouldn't it be coming up soon?

3075
02:11:11,210 --> 02:11:13,120
Is the bath stage bad on Ryuguu Terminal?

3076
02:11:13,120 --> 02:11:19,590
The bath stage has a lot of cover so it feels weak there

3077
02:11:19,590 --> 02:11:25,620
Kinmedai is great because you can splash down from the high ground, so it feels good~

3078
02:11:25,620 --> 02:11:28,570
Right? Yeah

3079
02:11:28,570 --> 02:11:32,570
Wheee~! So fun~!

3080
02:11:36,430 --> 02:11:39,840
Oh! It's here! Kinmedai! Nice! Amazing!

3081
02:11:39,840 --> 02:11:43,600
There's a jinx that it never goes the weird way

3082
02:11:43,600 --> 02:11:45,280
Haha, true

3083
02:11:45,280 --> 02:11:46,190
Oh, they're glowing

3084
02:11:46,190 --> 02:11:47,510
Sparkling

3085
02:11:47,510 --> 02:11:49,710
Oh everyone's glowing, everyone's glowing

3086
02:11:49,710 --> 02:11:52,710
The other team has good synergy too

3087
02:11:52,710 --> 02:11:54,990
Fresh

3088
02:11:54,990 --> 02:11:56,860
Yes, they're glowing

3089
02:11:56,860 --> 02:12:00,330
Alright, we're gonna roll them on the bath stage

3090
02:12:00,330 --> 02:12:03,030
We're gonna roll them hard

3091
02:12:03,030 --> 02:12:03,990
Watch out, there's someone with a long range weapon

3092
02:12:03,990 --> 02:12:05,850
Ugh, damn it, damn it all~

3093
02:12:05,850 --> 02:12:07,470
There's a bath stage player coming from the left

3094
02:12:07,470 --> 02:12:08,470
Yes

3095
02:12:08,470 --> 02:12:09,270
Yes~

3096
02:12:09,270 --> 02:12:10,270
Yes~

3097
02:12:10,270 --> 02:12:12,180
So who's coming from the right?

3098
02:12:12,180 --> 02:12:13,870
Hmm?

3099
02:12:13,870 --> 02:12:14,870
Let's think about it!

3100
02:12:14,870 --> 02:12:15,870
There's an N-ZAP on the right

3101
02:12:15,870 --> 02:12:18,670
There's an N-ZAP on the right!

3102
02:12:18,670 --> 02:12:20,470
Maybe a Gal?

3103
02:12:20,470 --> 02:12:21,470
Hmm

3104
02:12:21,470 --> 02:12:23,470
The bath stage player is doing the exact same thing

3105
02:12:23,470 --> 02:12:25,270
Ugh~

3106
02:12:25,270 --> 02:12:26,270
Stop it~

3107
02:12:26,270 --> 02:12:27,270
Everyone has such long range, I hate it

3108
02:12:27,270 --> 02:12:28,270
So annoying

3109
02:12:28,270 --> 02:12:29,270
True

3110
02:12:29,270 --> 02:12:30,270
Ughhh

3111
02:12:30,270 --> 02:12:31,270
Oh, there's a Goo Tuber~

3112
02:12:31,270 --> 02:12:34,070
I hate that there's a Goo Tuber~

3113
02:12:34,070 --> 02:12:35,070
Stop it, seriously stop it

3114
02:12:35,070 --> 02:12:37,070
Didn't you say Cyanide was a no-go?

3115
02:12:39,270 --> 02:12:42,070
Didn't you say Luten was good for dropping in?

3116
02:12:50,950 --> 02:12:52,950
Long range weapons are really rough

3117
02:12:54,750 --> 02:12:56,750
We didn't bring any long range weapons either

3118
02:12:56,750 --> 02:12:58,750
They might push in

3119
02:12:59,550 --> 02:13:00,550
They pushed in, one got through

3120
02:13:00,550 --> 02:13:02,550
Got taken out, sorry

3121
02:13:03,350 --> 02:13:04,350
It's okay.

3122
02:13:04,350 --> 02:13:06,220
Oh no, but they left, they left, they left!

3123
02:13:06,220 --> 02:13:09,150
Okay? I think our Ofuro... just dropped in.

3124
02:13:09,450 --> 02:13:12,950
Ofuro was being annoying, so I think they came to kill me. I see.

3125
02:13:12,950 --> 02:13:14,950
Ah, I see. Yeah.

3126
02:13:16,800 --> 02:13:18,800
Hmm, what should I do~?

3127
02:13:19,100 --> 02:13:21,600
No, like, yeah, right, right.

3128
02:13:22,400 --> 02:13:26,400
From the high ground, two on high ground right now. Yeah, mm-hmm, mm-hmm.

3129
02:13:26,400 --> 02:13:28,400
Whoa, what the heck was that?!

3130
02:13:29,200 --> 02:13:30,640
Ugh~.

3131
02:13:30,640 --> 02:13:34,000
Crab Meat. Quick Bomb, oh no~. Inking is so fun.

3132
02:13:34,000 --> 02:13:35,800
What should I do, what's the right way to go here?

3133
02:13:35,800 --> 02:13:36,800
Trade, trade!

3134
02:13:36,800 --> 02:13:37,800
Trade — nice?

3135
02:13:37,800 --> 02:13:39,600
Got the Jet Squelcher!

3136
02:13:39,600 --> 02:13:40,600
Nice!

3137
02:13:40,600 --> 02:13:41,400
From below!

3138
02:13:41,400 --> 02:13:42,400
Nice, nice!

3139
02:13:45,490 --> 02:13:46,490
Don't mess with me!

3140
02:13:48,290 --> 02:13:49,290
There!

3141
02:13:49,290 --> 02:13:51,090
Get over here!

3142
02:13:52,890 --> 02:13:54,890
Throw the Splat Bomb!

3143
02:13:58,360 --> 02:14:01,360
The range is just way too short, I can't do anything.

3144
02:14:03,140 --> 02:14:10,740
Heave-ho, heave-ho, heave-ho, heave-ho, heave-ho.

3145
02:14:10,740 --> 02:14:14,340
Heave-ho, heave-ho, heave-ho, heave-ho.

3146
02:14:14,340 --> 02:14:19,740
Heave-ho, heave-ho, heave-ho, heave-ho.

3147
02:14:19,740 --> 02:14:27,340
Heave-ho, heave-ho, heave-ho, heave-ho.

3148
02:14:27,340 --> 02:14:29,140
What? Who?

3149
02:14:29,140 --> 02:14:31,140
Got taken out. Oh, Ofuro's coming down.

3150
02:14:31,140 --> 02:14:32,940
Okay~!

3151
02:14:32,940 --> 02:14:34,940
Did we get Ofuro? Nice!

3152
02:14:34,940 --> 02:14:36,940
That's huge, that's huge!

3153
02:14:36,940 --> 02:14:38,940
Oh no, it wasn't Ofuro. What was that just now?

3154
02:14:38,940 --> 02:14:40,740
What was that just now?

3155
02:14:40,740 --> 02:14:42,740
What did you do just now?

3156
02:14:42,740 --> 02:14:44,540
What did I do just now?

3157
02:14:44,540 --> 02:14:46,340
What on earth did I just do?

3158
02:14:46,340 --> 02:14:48,140
Dropped down from the center.

3159
02:14:48,140 --> 02:14:50,140
Okay.

3160
02:14:50,140 --> 02:14:51,940
Was that bad?

3161
02:14:51,940 --> 02:14:53,940
What was that just now?

3162
02:14:53,940 --> 02:14:57,800
Well, I mean, this kind of thing happens sometimes.

3163
02:14:57,800 --> 02:15:01,460
It happens sometimes.

3164
02:15:01,460 --> 02:15:06,960
But it wasn't a total blowout at all — not a total blowout!

3165
02:15:06,960 --> 02:15:10,500
What percentage counts as a total blowout?

3166
02:15:10,500 --> 02:15:12,760
What percentage... hmm, what percent...

3167
02:15:12,760 --> 02:15:15,660
If it was like 19%, that's not a total blowout.

3168
02:15:15,660 --> 02:15:17,280
That's a pretty high bar.

3169
02:15:17,280 --> 02:15:18,820
Pretty much.

3170
02:15:18,820 --> 02:15:22,800
If it's around 20%, you'd say we put up a decent fight, right?

3171
02:15:22,800 --> 02:15:24,520
We fought hard, we fought hard!

3172
02:15:24,520 --> 02:15:29,620
I mean, Mio-sha, you've had a break from the game, right?

3173
02:15:29,620 --> 02:15:31,420
Wait, are you saying it's my fault?

3174
02:15:31,420 --> 02:15:32,620
No no no no!

3175
02:15:32,620 --> 02:15:37,480
I mean, you're still holding your own despite being rusty?

3176
02:15:37,800 --> 02:15:38,880
That's amazing, right?

3177
02:15:39,180 --> 02:15:40,120
Exactly!

3178
02:15:40,120 --> 02:15:44,180
Well, yeah, I mean — I've been playing for 8 hours now though.

3179
02:15:44,180 --> 02:15:45,360
That's true.

3180
02:15:45,360 --> 02:15:48,600
I've been playing for 8 hours, you know.

3181
02:15:48,600 --> 02:15:50,960
But still, Korone is the most warmed up out of everyone here.

3182
02:15:50,960 --> 02:15:51,600
That's right.

3183
02:15:51,600 --> 02:15:53,260
Yeah, I guess I am warmed up.

3184
02:15:53,260 --> 02:15:54,500
Yeah, yeah!

3185
02:15:54,500 --> 02:15:57,300
Flare and IRyS haven't played in like 10 months either.

3186
02:15:57,300 --> 02:15:57,980
10 months, that's wild.

3187
02:15:57,980 --> 02:16:00,240
You were doing Salmon Run the whole time, right?

3188
02:16:00,240 --> 02:16:00,640
Yeah.

3189
02:16:00,640 --> 02:16:01,640
Salmon Runner.

3190
02:16:01,640 --> 02:16:04,620
You must've saved up a lot of gold, right?

3191
02:16:06,040 --> 02:16:06,520
Great effort!

3192
02:16:06,520 --> 02:16:08,300
Saved up gold?

3193
02:16:09,500 --> 02:16:10,900
What do you even get from it?

3194
02:16:12,100 --> 02:16:12,420
Like...

3195
02:16:12,420 --> 02:16:14,600
Scales and stuff?

3196
02:16:14,600 --> 02:16:16,540
And gear and stuff?

3197
02:16:16,540 --> 02:16:18,540
Gear and name plates and stuff?

3198
02:16:18,540 --> 02:16:20,340
Do you do it because you want that stuff?

3199
02:16:20,340 --> 02:16:24,340
Or do you do it because Salmon Run itself is fun?

3200
02:16:24,340 --> 02:16:28,140
Most of what you get from Salmon Run is gear.

3201
02:16:28,140 --> 02:16:29,140
It's mostly gear

3202
02:16:29,140 --> 02:16:31,140
Yeah, pretty much just gear

3203
02:16:31,140 --> 02:16:32,940
Gear fragments too

3204
02:16:32,940 --> 02:16:33,940
I see

3205
02:16:33,940 --> 02:16:36,930
What I really want is the gold plate

3206
02:16:38,740 --> 02:16:40,540
Like the overall outfit? Is that what everyone wants?

3207
02:16:40,540 --> 02:16:42,460
Yeah, that's what I want

3208
02:16:42,460 --> 02:16:44,340
The enemy's got range!

3209
02:16:44,340 --> 02:16:45,140
No way!

3210
02:16:45,140 --> 02:16:46,140
They've got reach

