Go ahead, go ahead!

4274
03:02:27,540 --> 03:02:29,390
Hmm

4275
03:02:29,810 --> 03:02:33,830
This is my first time — first time riding the mikoshi

4276
03:02:33,830 --> 03:02:40,510
Wait, wasn't the mikoshi in Splatoon 2? Oh right, it wasn't... awww

4277
03:02:40,510 --> 03:02:45,450
My heart jumped — I thought gold came out, but it was silver! Awww!

4278
03:02:45,450 --> 03:02:55,010
Not gold, it was silver — and it was even a silver base title! What's the title for anyway?

4279
03:02:55,230 --> 03:02:58,450
Oh, it's tricky — does that mean we get a good banner?

4280
03:02:58,450 --> 03:03:02,790
Wait, how exactly do you ride it?

4281
03:03:02,790 --> 03:03:05,050
So, to ride the mikoshi...

4282
03:03:05,050 --> 03:03:08,260
Oh, there it is!

4283
03:03:08,260 --> 03:03:09,970
Amazing!

4284
03:03:09,970 --> 03:03:12,920
You go to the voting area? Where's the voting area?

4285
03:03:12,920 --> 03:03:18,280
It's the monitor where you chose your T-shirt and stuff at the beginning

4286
03:03:18,280 --> 03:03:21,060
Oh, it's the one on the side of the lobby, right?

4287
03:03:21,060 --> 03:03:24,220
No, not that one — it's in the plaza

4288
03:03:24,220 --> 03:03:27,240
The plaza where you voted when you got your T-shirt

4289
03:03:27,600 --> 03:03:30,880
The monitor near where the T-shirts are

4290
03:03:31,980 --> 03:03:35,280
The monitor where you chose your technique

4291
03:03:35,540 --> 03:03:36,540
Right, where I chose

4292
03:03:36,780 --> 03:03:38,820
And then at that monitor

4293
03:03:38,830 --> 03:03:40,920
You tap it

4294
03:03:41,160 --> 03:03:42,700
On the right side

4295
03:03:42,820 --> 03:03:45,500
Oh no, someone's telling me I'm in Splatsville

4296
03:03:45,500 --> 03:03:47,540
What? What does that mean? What?

4297
03:03:47,620 --> 03:03:49,980
Huh? That's not the right area

4298
03:03:50,540 --> 03:03:52,180
Ah, yeah, that's...

4299
03:03:52,400 --> 03:03:54,220
You're in the wrong area

4300
03:03:54,220 --> 03:03:56,020
You're in the old area

4301
03:03:56,020 --> 03:03:58,020
Yeah, you can only ride it from that side

4302
03:03:58,020 --> 03:03:59,820
Oh, I see!

4303
03:03:59,820 --> 03:04:01,620
I didn't know that

4304
03:04:01,620 --> 03:04:03,620
How do I get back?

4305
03:04:03,620 --> 03:04:05,620
The station...

4306
03:04:05,620 --> 03:04:07,620
Got it! I need to go to Inkopolis Square

4307
03:04:07,620 --> 03:04:09,420
You figured it out?

4308
03:04:12,450 --> 03:04:14,450
I'm on the train right now

4309
03:04:16,250 --> 03:04:18,250
Oh, there's a train in this game

4310
03:04:20,250 --> 03:04:25,670
Wait, was there a train animation? I thought you just went straight there

4311
03:04:25,670 --> 03:04:30,540
There's something — and I'm even dozing off on the train

4312
03:04:30,840 --> 03:04:33,820
Oh wow, that's something

4313
03:04:33,820 --> 03:04:40,300
It feels like going to another world! What is this, that's so cool!

4314
03:04:40,700 --> 03:04:44,980
I was on the train — it's like a story started

4315
03:04:44,980 --> 03:04:46,980
It did, lol

4316
03:04:46,980 --> 03:04:48,980
Wait, have you not done the story mode?

4317
03:04:48,980 --> 03:04:50,780
I haven't

4318
03:04:50,780 --> 03:04:52,580
Ahh~

4319
03:04:52,580 --> 03:04:54,580
Alterna's...

4320
03:04:54,580 --> 03:04:56,580
Alterna's Hero Mode is starting

4321
03:04:56,580 --> 03:04:58,580
No way!?

4322
03:04:58,580 --> 03:05:00,580
Oh no, Mio-sha's Hero Mode started!

4323
03:05:00,580 --> 03:05:02,380
Mio-sha's Hero Mode—

4324
03:05:02,380 --> 03:05:04,380
I wanted to watch that!

4325
03:05:04,380 --> 03:05:06,380
Hero Mode is crazy!

4326
03:05:06,380 --> 03:05:08,380
I kind of wanted to see it...

4327
03:05:08,380 --> 03:05:10,180
Are you serious!?

4328
03:05:10,180 --> 03:05:12,180
They're saying Side Order started!

4329
03:05:12,180 --> 03:05:14,820
It was Side Order?

4330
03:05:14,820 --> 03:05:18,440
I thought it was regular Hero Mode!

4331
03:05:18,440 --> 03:05:21,240
Side Order is fun though!

4332
03:05:21,240 --> 03:05:22,540
Can I step away to use the restroom real quick?

4333
03:05:22,540 --> 03:05:23,820
Oh, I want to go too!

4334
03:05:23,820 --> 03:05:25,420
Go ahead!

4335
03:05:25,420 --> 03:05:28,520
Okay, everyone watch the omikoshi for me!

4336
03:05:28,520 --> 03:05:30,240
Omikoshi, omikoshi!

4337
03:05:30,240 --> 03:05:34,820
How do you ride it again?

4338
03:05:34,820 --> 03:05:36,280
Hmm...

4339
03:05:36,280 --> 03:05:37,120
Okay, here we go...

4340
03:05:37,120 --> 03:05:38,760
Omikoshi, omikoshi!

4341
03:05:38,760 --> 03:05:40,680
Of all things...

4342
03:05:40,680 --> 03:05:42,680
Something started happening...

4343
03:05:44,480 --> 03:05:46,280
What's going on— oh right,

4344
03:05:46,280 --> 03:05:47,080
Side Order, right?

4345
03:05:47,080 --> 03:05:48,080
What's Side Order like again?

4346
03:05:48,080 --> 03:05:51,080
It's that world painted all white, covered in white.

4347
03:05:51,080 --> 03:05:52,080
Oh right, right, the whitish one!

4348
03:05:52,080 --> 03:05:53,080
Yeah, yeah, exactly!

4349
03:05:53,880 --> 03:05:55,870
But I never finished it either, so...

4350
03:05:55,870 --> 03:05:56,680
Oh, really?

4351
03:05:56,680 --> 03:05:58,680
I don't think I ever finished Side Order.

4352
03:05:58,680 --> 03:06:00,680
It's fun but it's hard!

4353
03:06:01,480 --> 03:06:02,480
Yeah, yeah, yeah!

4354
03:06:02,480 --> 03:06:03,280
It really is hard, isn't it?

4355
03:06:03,280 --> 03:06:04,280
Umm...

4356
03:06:04,280 --> 03:06:05,080
I see.

4357
03:06:05,080 --> 03:06:06,080
Omikoshi, omikoshi!

4358
03:06:06,080 --> 03:06:08,080
Wait, how do you ride the omikoshi again?

4359
03:06:08,080 --> 03:06:11,480
A photo? Was it a photo?

4360
03:06:11,480 --> 03:06:14,480
No, that's not it...

4361
03:06:18,080 --> 03:06:19,880
There's some kind of robot here.

4362
03:06:21,680 --> 03:06:25,480
Ugh, how do I get back?

4363
03:06:25,480 --> 03:06:27,480
Reminiscing about Inkopolis...

4364
03:06:27,480 --> 03:06:31,480
I always left the photos to Fuu-tan whenever we rode the omikoshi, so...

4365
03:06:31,480 --> 03:06:33,480
I've completely forgotten how.

4366
03:06:33,480 --> 03:06:36,480
I never really did that part myself.

4367
03:06:36,480 --> 03:06:38,280
Oh, she's back!

4368
03:06:38,280 --> 03:06:40,280
The monitor— is it the monitor?

4369
03:06:40,280 --> 03:06:42,080
Hmm?

4370
03:06:43,670 --> 03:06:45,670
Welcome back!

4371
03:06:45,670 --> 03:06:47,470
Is it this?

4372
03:06:47,470 --> 03:06:49,270
In Splatsville...

4373
03:06:49,270 --> 03:06:51,070
Oh, this one— hold on.

4374
03:06:51,070 --> 03:06:53,950
I might have been going to the wrong place, at the station.

4375
03:06:53,950 --> 03:06:56,700
Go to Splatsville!

4376
03:06:58,470 --> 03:06:59,470
I'm back!

4377
03:06:59,470 --> 03:07:01,470
Mio-san, did you make it?

4378
03:07:01,470 --> 03:07:03,420
I did, I did, I did!

4379
03:07:03,420 --> 03:07:05,270
Looks like I was going to the wrong spot.

4380
03:07:07,070 --> 03:07:08,870
Yeah, yeah, yeah!

4381
03:07:08,870 --> 03:07:10,870
It's here, right?

4382
03:07:10,870 --> 03:07:12,870
The place with the big TV-like thing, right?

4383
03:07:12,870 --> 03:07:14,870
Welcome back!

4384
03:07:14,870 --> 03:07:16,870
I brought prosciutto!

4385
03:07:16,870 --> 03:07:18,870
Nice!

4386
03:07:18,870 --> 03:07:20,870
Very snack-like!

4387
03:07:20,870 --> 03:07:22,870
I can't eat prosciutto on its own though.

4388
03:07:22,870 --> 03:07:24,870
Wow, really?

4389
03:07:24,870 --> 03:07:26,870
You can't eat prosciutto as-is?

4390
03:07:26,870 --> 03:07:30,190
Without bread or crackers it's too salty to eat on its own.

4391
03:07:30,190 --> 03:07:32,170
Oh, I see!

4392
03:07:32,170 --> 03:07:34,570
Hmm, I kind of get that.

4393
03:07:34,570 --> 03:07:36,310
What about with melon?

4394
03:07:36,310 --> 03:07:37,750
I don't think I've ever had prosciutto with melon.

4395
03:07:37,750 --> 03:07:40,550
Prosciutto and melon together?

4396
03:07:40,550 --> 03:07:43,790
Mio-shi, press the Plus button there—

4397
03:07:43,790 --> 03:07:46,690
you can display names and stuff too!

4398
03:07:46,690 --> 03:07:50,670
Oh wow, really! Name display!

4399
03:07:50,670 --> 03:07:52,550
You know your stuff, Korone!

4400
03:07:52,550 --> 03:07:56,550
I just did the outfit thing earlier!

4401
03:07:56,550 --> 03:07:58,550
It's nice to have a name for it, right?

4402
03:07:58,550 --> 03:08:01,840
Yeah, nice!

4403
03:08:01,840 --> 03:08:04,640
That's great, that's great!

4404
03:08:04,640 --> 03:08:06,640
How do you get on the omikoshi float?

4405
03:08:06,640 --> 03:08:09,440
No way, IRyS!

4406
03:08:09,440 --> 03:08:11,440
Aren't you in a weird spot too, maybe?

4407
03:08:11,440 --> 03:08:13,240
No, no!

4408
03:08:13,240 --> 03:08:14,240
How do you get on this thing?

4409
03:08:14,240 --> 03:08:16,240
Toward the monitor—

4410
03:08:16,240 --> 03:08:17,240
So cute!

4411
03:08:17,240 --> 03:08:18,240
So cute!

4412
03:08:18,240 --> 03:08:20,240
Go back, go back, go back once!

4413
03:08:20,240 --> 03:08:25,340
Stop the camera, press the poster button toward the monitor—

4414
03:08:25,340 --> 03:08:27,100
Then go right.

4415
03:08:27,100 --> 03:08:29,740
Ahhh!

4416
03:08:29,740 --> 03:08:31,580
Yes yes yes yes yes!

4417
03:08:31,580 --> 03:08:32,680
Oh I see!

4418
03:08:32,680 --> 03:08:34,420
Oh, so that's how you do it!

4419
03:08:34,420 --> 03:08:35,600
Yes yes yes yes yes!

4420
03:08:35,600 --> 03:08:37,760
How many years have you been playing Splatfest?

4421
03:08:37,760 --> 03:08:40,540
I always left the photos to Flare.

4422
03:08:40,540 --> 03:08:44,760
And here's the woman who won 333x saying that...

4423
03:08:44,760 --> 03:08:46,670
I don't remember any of it!

4424
03:08:46,670 --> 03:08:54,100
The photo... like this? Nice! That was the best!

4425
03:08:53,900 --> 03:08:57,420
Mio-san looks like she's about to wrap up.

4426
03:08:57,420 --> 03:09:00,700
Wait, apparently someone just hit the jackpot on the lottery—

4427
03:09:00,700 --> 03:09:01,800
Wait, seriously? What?

4428
03:09:01,800 --> 03:09:04,280
Something popped up on screen—

4429
03:09:04,280 --> 03:09:05,760
I don't think it's me though.

4430
03:09:05,760 --> 03:09:08,720
It's Carbonara who hit the jackpot on the lottery.

4431
03:09:08,720 --> 03:09:09,980
Ah, so that's what it was!

4432
03:09:09,980 --> 03:09:10,700
Nice!

4433
03:09:10,500 --> 03:09:13,200
That's the silver one from earlier.

4434
03:09:13,200 --> 03:09:15,890
But it's not gold though.

4435
03:09:15,890 --> 03:09:17,820
I've never gotten gold even once.

4436
03:09:17,820 --> 03:09:20,120
She's the lottery winner!

4437
03:09:20,120 --> 03:09:21,060
Carbonara!

4438
03:09:21,060 --> 03:09:24,980
If it's not gold, it doesn't count as a winning gold ticket.

4439
03:09:24,980 --> 03:09:29,180
Then let's keep going until we get gold!

4440
03:09:29,180 --> 03:09:35,840
During Flare's streams when we played together, gold came out like twice, right?

4441
03:09:35,840 --> 03:09:37,420
Really?

4442
03:09:37,420 --> 03:09:39,300
I think we only played together once though.

4443
03:09:39,300 --> 03:09:42,700
Hmm, but I feel like gold came out once before too...

4444
03:09:42,700 --> 03:09:44,600
So gold really doesn't come out that often, huh.

4445
03:09:44,600 --> 03:09:46,900
Flare really is lucky!

4446
03:09:46,900 --> 03:09:50,100
She's probably gotten it like 3 or 4 times total.

4447
03:09:50,100 --> 03:09:53,900
Ah, it came out when she played solo, but—

4448
03:09:53,900 --> 03:09:56,500
When she played with IRyS, I think it was only once.

4449
03:09:56,500 --> 03:09:58,200
Hmm~

4450
03:09:58,200 --> 03:09:59,400
That's not many~

4451
03:09:59,400 --> 03:10:03,700
I want a gold ticket, a gold ticket!

4452
03:10:03,700 --> 03:10:05,000
She's begging for one!

4453
03:10:06,800 --> 03:10:07,420
Should I give her one?

4454
03:10:07,420 --> 03:10:09,360
Give it to me, give it to me!

4455
03:10:09,360 --> 03:10:11,020
I already used mine up.

4456
03:10:11,020 --> 03:10:13,020
Give it to me!

4457
03:10:13,820 --> 03:10:15,760
Why not me...

4458
03:10:16,620 --> 03:10:18,620
Is everyone feeling like wrapping up?

4459
03:10:19,420 --> 03:10:22,370
I just ate the new coin thing.

4460
03:10:22,370 --> 03:10:24,050
New coin?

4461
03:10:24,050 --> 03:10:26,820
Yeah, the one that gives you more coins — I just ate it.

4462
03:10:26,820 --> 03:10:27,820
Oh, nice!

4463
03:10:27,820 --> 03:10:29,620
Oh, I ate one too!

4464
03:10:30,620 --> 03:10:32,960
With Mio-sha's schedule tomorrow and all—

4465
03:10:32,960 --> 03:10:34,280
Yeah, that's true for Mio-sha.

4466
03:10:34,280 --> 03:10:36,900
She'll have to leave, huh.

4467
03:10:36,900 --> 03:10:38,600
Well, I mean—

4468
03:10:38,600 --> 03:10:39,900
Until around 2 o'clock.

4469
03:10:39,900 --> 03:10:41,280
You can stay until 2?

4470
03:10:42,780 --> 03:10:44,220
That's great, that's great!

4471
03:10:44,220 --> 03:10:46,900
I'll totally stick around, no problem!

4472
03:10:46,900 --> 03:10:50,940
I don't know why I'm being dragged into this.

4473
03:10:50,940 --> 03:10:52,520
I'll totally stay, really!

4474
03:10:52,520 --> 03:10:53,500
The way she applies pressure...

4475
03:10:53,500 --> 03:10:55,980
She's a pro at applying pressure.

4476
03:10:55,980 --> 03:10:57,620
I made one!

4477
03:10:57,620 --> 03:10:59,420
Yay!

4478
03:10:59,420 --> 03:11:02,420
I changed the BGM — will everyone hear it?

4479
03:11:04,460 --> 03:11:05,260
BGM?

4480
03:11:05,260 --> 03:11:07,260
Yeah, I changed the BGM on my end.

4481
03:11:07,260 --> 03:11:08,180
You can change it?

4482
03:11:08,180 --> 03:11:09,060
Yeah, you can change it

4483
03:11:09,060 --> 03:11:09,860
Huh?

4484
03:11:09,860 --> 03:11:11,460
For 100 yen

4485
03:11:11,460 --> 03:11:13,260
Wait, what?

4486
03:11:13,260 --> 03:11:15,260
Huh? What are you talking about?

4487
03:11:15,260 --> 03:11:17,860
Is the BGM playing? In the lobby?

4488
03:11:17,860 --> 03:11:19,860
It sounds like the usual BGM to me

4489
03:11:19,860 --> 03:11:21,520
Oh, it's after you go in

4490
03:11:21,520 --> 03:11:23,460
Wait, how do you change it?

4491
03:11:23,460 --> 03:11:30,260
Isn't there a jukebox to the right of the shop area?

4492
03:11:30,260 --> 03:11:31,060
What about the back of the shop?

4493
03:11:31,060 --> 03:11:33,060
Now that you mention it, yeah there is

4494
03:11:33,060 --> 03:11:34,860
But I can't interact with it

4495
03:11:34,860 --> 03:11:37,660
You can only change it before you enter

4496
03:11:37,660 --> 03:11:38,660
Oh really?

4497
03:11:38,660 --> 03:11:39,660
I see

4498
03:11:39,660 --> 03:11:45,460
Does the jukebox change take effect in the next match after you set it? When does it change?

4499
03:11:45,460 --> 03:11:47,260
This is bad

4500
03:11:48,450 --> 03:11:51,490
Right now I've got it set to the Splatoon 2 ending BGM

4501
03:11:51,490 --> 03:11:53,490
Oh wow

4502
03:11:53,490 --> 03:11:55,290
Honestly, for me

4503
03:11:55,290 --> 03:11:57,090
When it comes to Splatoon

4504
03:11:57,090 --> 03:12:00,090
Outside of the actual matches and gameplay

4505
03:12:00,090 --> 03:12:04,090
I'm actually not that knowledgeable about it

4506
03:12:04,090 --> 03:12:05,890
I haven't really explored much

4507
03:12:05,890 --> 03:12:07,690
Oh really?

4508
03:12:07,690 --> 03:12:09,490
Negitaro!

4509
03:12:09,490 --> 03:12:11,490
Negitaro is insane!

4510
03:12:11,490 --> 03:12:14,350
Isn't Negitaro crazy?

4511
03:12:14,350 --> 03:12:15,290
I hate Negitaro so much

4512
03:12:15,290 --> 03:12:17,290
If I hate their loadout, that means everyone hates it too

4513
03:12:17,290 --> 03:12:19,290
There's a Liter too

4514
03:12:19,290 --> 03:12:21,090
Where is this again?

4515
03:12:21,090 --> 03:12:23,090
I don't remember

4516
03:12:23,090 --> 03:12:25,090
It'll come back to me once I play

4517
03:12:25,090 --> 03:12:27,090
This is one of the stages added in Splatoon 3

4518
03:12:27,090 --> 03:12:29,090
But you played Splatoon 3, right?

4519
03:12:29,090 --> 03:12:30,890
Maybe a little after Splatoon 3 came out

4520
03:12:30,890 --> 03:12:32,890
I joined pretty late into it

4521
03:12:32,890 --> 03:12:34,890
There's a real chance I've never seen this stage

4522
03:12:34,890 --> 03:12:36,890
Seriously?

4523
03:12:36,890 --> 03:12:38,690
It's the one where the middle moves

4524
03:12:38,690 --> 03:12:40,490
Just a moment

4525
03:12:40,490 --> 03:12:42,290
Liters and stuff are pretty strong here

4526
03:12:42,290 --> 03:12:44,450
There's a pretty strong elevator section too

4527
03:12:44,450 --> 03:12:47,310
Ah, so it's a stage suited for long-range weapons

4528
03:12:47,310 --> 03:12:49,670
Yeah, right in the middle

4529
03:12:49,670 --> 03:12:51,390
The rail floor on one side is nice

4530
03:12:51,390 --> 03:12:52,470
Nice!

4531
03:12:52,470 --> 03:12:58,920
Ugh, got killed

4532
03:12:58,920 --> 03:13:00,280
By a Carbon Roller

4533
03:13:00,280 --> 03:13:02,640
The area isn't that big

4534
03:13:02,640 --> 03:13:04,360
So comebacks happen pretty easily

4535
03:13:04,360 --> 03:13:05,140
Oh really?

4536
03:13:05,140 --> 03:13:08,560
Okay

4537
03:13:08,560 --> 03:13:13,440
I'm gonna go put some pressure on that Liter Charger — nice!

4538
